  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, an Aura3D orrery, and it passes typecheck. I couldn't run it in a browser or build it with `vite build`, so I haven't seen a rendered frame. Light intensity, bloom strength and ring orientation are untested guesses.\n\n- **Star:** a bright emissive sphere at the centre. It has a warm point light and a bloom effect (`effects.bloom`).\n- **Planets:** five of different sizes and colours on radii 2.8 to 9. Their orbital speeds range from 1.2 down to 0.22 rad/s. An `onFrame` callback moves them every frame with `setPosition`, so frames differ over time.\n- **Ring:** the fourth planet (`saturn`) has a tilted ring. It is a thin flattened torus grouped with the planet, so it moves with it.\n- **Background and orbits:** the background is near-black (`#02030a`), with faint torus lines marking each orbit.\n- **Camera:** a perspective camera at [0, 15, 17] looks down at the origin and should frame all orbits.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` plus two animation frames.\n\n",
